How to get the old loader back (best and fastest way)
Your host simply.com automatically saves daily backups of your entire site for several weeks. You can restore the old index.html yourself in 2–3 minutes for free.
Step-by-step:

Log into your simply.com kontrolpanel (the normal login where you manage domains, email, etc.).
Click on Website (or “Hjemmeside” if it’s in Danish).
Look for the button Genskab data or Restore data.
Choose a backup date before you did the update (e.g. 20 March 2026, 19 March, or earlier — the backups run every night around 01–03).
You can restore the whole root folder or just select the single file index.html (simply.com lets you pick specific files/folders).
Confirm and restore.

After the restore:

Your old nice loading page with the iframe will be back as index.html.
The game will still be in spil.html (or wherever it was before).
Everything will work exactly like before the update.

If the backup is too new or you can’t find the old version

Check your own computer:
Search for old downloads of index.html (you probably downloaded the site before uploading the update).
Check Time Machine (Mac), File History (Windows), Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, or any folder where you keep website backups.
Look in your email — you might have sent yourself the old loader file at some point.

